  "contentHtml": "<p>These are in the order I read them, and behind the link is either my post on the book or simply the Amazon page:</p>\n<p>Alan Allport, <a href=\"https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2026/01/sectoral-shifts-in-supply-wartime-agriculture-edition.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Advance Britannia: The Epic Story of the Second World War, 1942-1945</a>.</p>\n<p>Anna Arno, <a href=\"https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2026/02/paul-celan-a-life-by-anna-arno.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Paul Celan: A Life</a>.</p>\n<p>Brendan Greeley, <a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Almighty-Dollar-Years-Worlds-Powerful/dp/0593138880/ref=sr_1_1?crid=2JBA1VCFA4GH2&amp;dib=eyJ2IjoiMSJ9.pvMfVrPcVaK6alkVnhbQUSDLRoH9PYnAtLXVjUzcXTXCjjsNffRAfiGXoHK9f9B3yBpoOnautfKtpVr00t-BE0HKzQ_HQMa6pz7gsCRdbL_8uDz72DUJhkHwUtsTqpL3yCCTncVWNyPb4kQUZnCHCnA8z9RJC0AggHwcT9MgJJQQOsTACibg_tGmI2xsOL2U6WHJKeK7xK6yRwaMOonA8zhBUp8p0sHFUtXPoA8q9Mk.MNmwlAE8K6CRnpk9Ygd1ckx4TuxccW_5G1Zp-nZuORk&amp;dib_tag=se&amp;keywords=The+Almighty+Dollar%3A+500+Years+of+the+World%27s+Most+Powerful+Money&amp;nsdOptOutParam=true&amp;qid=1794768765&amp;sprefix=the+almighty+dollar+500+years+of+the+world%27s+most+powerful+money%2Caps%2C178&amp;sr=8-1\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">The Almighty Dollar: 500 Years of the World’s Most Powerful Money</a>.</p>\n<p>Sebastian Mallaby, <a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Infinity-Machine-Hassabis-DeepMind-Superintelligence/dp/0593831845/ref=sr_1_1?crid=MQGG5PVDXF87&amp;dib=eyJ2IjoiMSJ9.3QJ7KZeO3wqmeUgn8u9ykxDsVqJr-J5vXU62XEZzZwED31hVtrWp_fb1rtvRJp8b5-xSQdBprooY8ryYs5uKkwNHkCf7kronr2_pk6SBTrUtuQyrdUvbOtOBYAw8RvleFGq94xgp1Pnjxom1zIJsPmp9ADugY6TiF5b_3yanN4jJYZ8FLgMO1gZYXKoMVpkBtSZZfBOigh8GYjpgx0mF3ebcXGiSJei_15pQ1vNw_8E.OY7O5O7stJmIs4rRsnaiV_poJ74DpCMkBmriVO2BgEI&amp;dib_tag=se&amp;keywords=The+Infinity+Machine&amp;qid=1794768711&amp;sprefix=the+infinity+machine%2Caps%2C509&amp;sr=8-1\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">The Infinity Machine: Demis Hassabis, DeepMind, and the Quest for Superintelligence</a>.</p>\n<p>Mark B. Smith, <a href=\"https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2026/04/what-ive-been-reading-285.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Exit Stalin: The Soviet Union as a Civilization 1953-1991</a>.</p>\n<p>David Narrett, <a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cherokees-War-Peace-1670-1840/dp/0674306139/ref=sr_1_1?crid=GFPF8UCMNWZD&amp;dib=eyJ2IjoiMSJ9._4Qw_AOdumuMebXdDjv5yCCLsJqAtHwB1KTadYIXOzfvHNRNo9XggYUvHitmb8Jlds3w_LAL2NG7mhejGOJ7W3tmSg-APzGfILzGOg_AQf2uAJyN8gb_Ea0BnVfIkgbSBWxBWs3YK09BAVjBMlQJ3t4V1iEjfHLaCjyafMTb8Bvrf1pK9glZeEoqu6R8gfQ3ahEiVeZTPI1nlVjrJWFFN9HQHwuScEwgVol5IIG0rCE.cI7-_uBBGwZ2o107HIfwQ-hzOl5uvAlwde3mWD4vXUI&amp;dib_tag=se&amp;keywords=The+Cherokees+in+War+%26+At+Peace+1670-1840&amp;nsdOptOutParam=true&amp;qid=1794768812&amp;sprefix=the+cherokees+in+war+%26+at+peace+1670-1840%2Caps%2C791&amp;sr=8-1\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">The Cherokees in War &amp; At Peace 1670-1840</a>.</p>\n<p>Victoria Whitworth, <a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Book-Kells-Landmark-Library/dp/1788541804/ref=sr_1_1?crid=28NDZ9AX50S5Q&amp;dib=eyJ2IjoiMSJ9.vFgx2e2yQwnF6kP1CaFbOA.GAGZx6an34HgKzjdfwm_RP6lEVw9nHW0fTGV6cclkco&amp;dib_tag=se&amp;keywords=the+book+of+kells+unlocking+the+enigma+by+victoria+whitworth&amp;nsdOptOutParam=true&amp;qid=1783362728&amp;sprefix=victoria+whitworth%2Caps%2C206&amp;sr=8-1\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">The Book of Kells: Unlocking the Enigma</a>.</p>\n<p>Tom Grifffiths, <a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Laws-Thought-Quest-Mathematical-Theory/dp/1250358353/ref=sr_1_2?crid=11WI11L2F0X64&amp;dib=eyJ2IjoiMSJ9.S2iKQbVnNZ-KvnXckCfXGGcdPMRSLv0-QTKYvSBpXpKvoDHZROGBfKo0Mlx2pKEulbujI6589Rm1XulppI1o-KbaV5fPNlILUusS8zNtkgx0x_LASuvfRw8MNAAsjf6L35yNxru1pmAD_Q9n0HDq-5dvoLK4QcSUgXJeRzP45g6dyuJbGnJ5HQ8xgdLVDaiiSKqNf3_3Qca-m3lBWl4c6WqFfQmoJHhXJPudCluGrzo.T_v_HIsrwJhoHwQqSHxQJx4FrlJSl1TEcMENp7-beEs&amp;dib_tag=se&amp;keywords=tom+griffiths&amp;qid=1794769409&amp;sprefix=tom+griffiths%2Caps%2C886&amp;sr=8-2\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">The Laws of Thought: The Quest for a Mathematical Theory of the Mind</a>.</p>\n<p>Vasily Grossman, <a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Front-Line-Stalingrad-Treblinka-Berlin-1941-45/dp/B0F7G427YD/ref=sr_1_1?crid=3V5WG1V7UVTF9&amp;dib=eyJ2IjoiMSJ9.kUM9IZPMjvHihhy6GZEmOj9LVcsA3Q0zrOAN60MshFuWS7-vN2UMnXvgoMhZMlzdPy5m0OJKYw__OJDyTWQ2wfDV3r7K8LEFE_jIKemH7W4q3E4n1c34v1IiB40Klz4cMakps_d85iBwG68K3E6WJTGlGbCIxnhSmqfKZG1oeaqtXzmFR6-IzNVv6jswfoARxjdiE_df9lRrKh5qrmfKSeSeu0YXmAjENrNDMPM_g2o.7d0G8gCwpCsFelittZOKU4cpj4aqI_PpZRUwHNy8D8c&amp;dib_tag=se&amp;keywords=From+the+Front+Line%2C+Stalingrad-Treblinka-Berlin+1941-1945&amp;qid=1794768843&amp;sprefix=from+the+front+line%2C+stalingrad-treblinka-berlin+1941-1945%2Caps%2C531&amp;sr=8-1\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">From the Front Line, Stalingrad-Treblinka-Berlin 1941-1945</a>.</p>\n<p>Tim Whitmarsh, <a href=\"https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2026/08/romes-age-of-revolution.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Rome’s Age of Revolution: Augustus, Empire, and the Making of Christianity</a>.</p>\n<p>Peter Gray, <a href=\"https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2026/08/restoring-childhood-how-to-set-kids-free-in-the-age-of-anxiety.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Restoring Childhood: How to Set Kids Free in the Age of Anxiety</a>.</p>\n<p>Michael Khodarkovsky, <a href=\"https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2026/08/that-was-then-this-is-now-60.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">The Steppe and its Empires: The Russian Empire &amp; its Eurasian Counterparts</a>.</p>\n<p>Patrick Wyman, <a href=\"https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2026/10/lost-worlds.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Lost Worlds: </a><span id=\"productTitle\">How Humans Tried, Failed, Succeeded, and Built Our World – A History of Civilization Through Trial and Error, Ice Age to Bronze Age.</span></p>\n<p>Jonathan Parshall, <a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/1942-Crux-War-Jonathan-Parshall/dp/0197848370/ref=sr_1_1?crid=2UFWEHVZ29OZY&amp;dib=eyJ2IjoiMSJ9.t9qCoa6xqaWN_IJRL_v6D8YsHtdZysQRjhyTl1587OeZxO0tQjAjIUhUquuh0AuyAbkuilLuED4hOrgutZT0OkH2heOUoBr_lMcKiTR1NcqFTY7gT8OfYyNMqhU_DLKMs0Un6Lyj4JgNMwYtpOgDb6f-auIa0fz-RgybzhJaGZLB0Q_8VRyLaUyrIizZX76ElG8bQEvV5KgUfSvy1QhW2eiNomfIdgQVi877ngf-oqs.4x8n12v1SsF0Aw0pVzeTiHlBmLGWgNcWlE59oo2pARE&amp;dib_tag=se&amp;keywords=1942%3A+Crux+of+War&amp;qid=1794769487&amp;sprefix=1942+crux+of+war%2Caps%2C279&amp;sr=8-1\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">1942: Crux of War</a> (I have only read part of this one, it is very long).</p>\n<p>Overall this year had, in terms of quantity, less to offer than most years?&nbsp; There is a market recession for publishing intelligent non-fiction, though I am not sure whether that is the relevant cause here, given how niche my interests can be.</p>\n<p>Of all those, my number one pick would be Anna Arno, <a href=\"https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2026/02/paul-celan-a-life-by-anna-arno.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Paul Celan: A Life</a>, by far the best book on one of our greatest poets, and a look at how personal lives operate as well.&nbsp; Here <a href=\"https://www.commonreader.co.uk/p/philosophy-celan-teresa-joyce-theory?utm_source=post-email-title&amp;publication_id=120973&amp;post_id=224471062&amp;utm_campaign=email-post-title&amp;isFreemail=true&amp;r=3o9&amp;triedRedirect=true&amp;utm_medium=email\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Henry Oliver covers the book</a> (and others as well):</p>\n<blockquote><p>What a splendid, splendid book. Adorno said that “To write poetry after Auschwitz is barbaric.” Celan proved him wrong. Naturally, this is a difficult subject matter to read about: not the sort of book you ought to read if you are sitting up alone at night. Arno has everything a biographer ought to have: mastery of the details, sensitive feeling for the poetry, and a calm controlled narrative style, so that the horrors and traumas can be dealt with properly, as can the ordinary aspects of life. This will be (one of) the best work(s) of literary non-fiction published this year. I don’t find Celan easy to apprehend in translation and I learned a lot from this book.</p></blockquote>\n<p>Recommended.&nbsp; And here are <a href=\"https://marginalrevolution.com/?s=best+non-fiction\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">previous installments in this series</a>, I do one each year.&nbsp; I like it to appear right before the peak of shopping season, and will write an addendum for what comes out between now and year’s end.</p>\n<p>What else might be on the list?</p>",
